{
  "title": "TextView undo history and single-allocation replacement: matched allocation traces",
  "platform": "macOS 15.7.9 arm64; Nim 2.4.0",
  "workload": "One fresh process per case. An 8 MiB ASCII source is held alive; the TextView receives single-character insertions. Styled cases change font size on half the source. Undo and redo cases replay all 32 edits.",
  "method": "MALLOC stack logging enabled before process launch. At the post-operation checkpoint, leaks --fullStackHistory --outputGraph=<file> <pid> and malloc_history <file> -highWaterMark -callTree -invert -ignoreThreads -consolidateAllBySymbol and without -highWaterMark. Each case is one traced sample. Apple tool units are preserved. The tracked capture driver reproduces the checkpoint and keeps a bounded wait and cleanup.",
  "limitations": [
    "Logged heap plus VM excludes allocations without stack records and differs from process RSS.",
    "One traced sample per case; logging changes timing and memory.",
    "The delta undo implementation reduces retained history but reconstructs whole flat text on replay; single-allocation replacement reduces that transient traffic but does not eliminate it."
  ],
  "harness": {
    "path": "tests/benchmarks/textundogroupallocationprobe.nim",
